{"posts":[{"id":"flaglimits_p18_426","t":"Aaron\n\nHi Macbow,\n\nI have made some comments on your FL homework, a few pointers for you to remember, also if you have not already, please do take a look at the FL article, and read the whole thread making notes\n\n1707\n\nAaron","a":"—","d":"","n":"#426","p":18,"im":["53ee7d2a9d886f8e046cda4e9ef6baddae7727d2","1c500735bc69486859d93545f74b5232a23f97ad","7d11f204fd5ca1a5220ee7f07447eca9c28117a5","5cce76b5b601511be61e6325b308eb26b9076633"],"m":426},{"id":"flaglimits_p18_427","t":"Wes\n\nFirst attempt on FLs.\n\nI'm not sure if they're correct FLs. I'm still a bit confused about FLs/FTRs. I've read something Harry posted in which he said that they are the same thing really.\n\nI will continue my homework on Flag Limits until it's completely clear to me!","a":"—","d":"","n":"#427","p":18,"im":["0a286d257753fb3fff372ea2eb0b735d2fa6e94b"],"m":427},{"id":"flaglimits_p18_428","t":"rcmacf\n\nI'd like to say (as Aaron's too modest) that his post just above, readthemarket.com/index.php/forum/homewo...mits?start=425#29938is an absolute peach, and one that will pay off hugely if you take the time to understand every comment on there.","a":"—","d":"","n":"#428","p":18,"im":[],"m":428},{"id":"flaglimits_p18_429","t":"Have been doing a lot of reading today. Aaron I appreciate your advice mate. Here is another FL that reacted somewhat differently from the others I have posted.","a":"—","d":"","n":"#429","p":18,"im":["0e8fa45d5e871bdb5f502f99d30fb405383c08cd"],"m":429},{"id":"flaglimits_p18_430","t":"OK...got to looking more at what the chart was saying. At B, price gave the heads up that it was going further up by engulfing A. It then did the the retrace to 4. Next itmade a lower high at C, again sucking the retail traders in by having them think price was going to drop, enabling them to keep on buying.","a":"—","d":"","n":"#430","p":18,"im":["60979281b35ad68c8eea39da1592176c50a0d911"],"m":430},{"id":"flaglimits_p18_431","t":"OK last one and I am off to ride the ponies...","a":"—","d":"","n":"#431","p":18,"im":["a1d212912cc50fb211123af7dd7630d3afb33889"],"m":431},{"id":"flaglimits_p18_432","t":"Wes\n\nSecond try:\n\nAdditional comment: because price engulfed the upper flag limit it is now free to move upwards.","a":"—","d":"","n":"#432","p":18,"im":["6f36c8fd1d15990d5a4b0b2cd2906bb153717ece"],"m":432},{"id":"flaglimits_p18_433","t":"Wes\n\nMore homework!\n\nI hope I'm spotting the right things. If not, please let me know!","a":"—","d":"","n":"#433","p":18,"im":["3865cacbefa4a820bac1d765d892d6b14f29e40b","ea2a736a5c63f0c81dafce18c461e4c66f7ca1f6","2db35579c1208f57cc380efa0e18c608fe14248d"],"m":433},{"id":"flaglimits_p18_434","t":"Aaron\n\nHi Wes,\n\nNice work mate! I have made some comments and asked a few questions on the chart, it may help\n\n1707","a":"—","d":"","n":"#434","p":18,"im":["7b1569d97162b00835deb619ee6fa6bb532dd046"],"m":434},{"id":"flaglimits_p18_435","t":"Wes\n\nThanks for reviewing my charts Aaron.\n\nHad another look at the chart with your comments. Meanwhile I will continue my search for FLs.","a":"—","d":"","n":"#435","p":18,"im":["d9a2d4c6ad9674ca02aa77247c943a8ee930ed2b"],"m":435},{"id":"flaglimits_p18_436","t":"Aaron\n\nHi Wes,\n\nNo problem, For me the answer you gave to my question was correct, remember FLs are continuation patterns, and NEED to engulf an SR, to make the FL valid.\n\nKeep posting mate!\n\nAaron\n\n1707","a":"—","d":"","n":"#436","p":18,"im":[],"m":436},{"id":"flaglimits_p18_437","t":"I have been doing more reading and went to looking at the latest move we have had on EJ. I have put together some charts of what I see happening.","a":"—","d":"","n":"#437","p":18,"im":["796223b2ca1ca300b334e85ac183aed3cef7418a","f4653d9f6f5f2f8d0ada89664d2a44d70c0701a3","468f10ebd65eab54321a13836f79c3a826dbc93e","4419cbe63cd6cafa624b6586039b90ab564db816"],"m":437},{"id":"flaglimits_p18_438","t":"I would love feedback on this one from someone if possible. This is EJ right now. From looking at the monthly chart, I would be thinking it is bullish and I think price will go higher, but not without a battle. Of course we can expect price to react off previous supply, but my question is exactly where should we be expecting the reaction with how the charts look. I think I have explained what I am looking at in my charts.\n\nThis is the daily chart. The purple area is from my previous post showing the origin of this move up.\n\nThis is the 1 h chart showing the origin of the last move down.","a":"—","d":"","n":"#438","p":18,"im":["c9544bf15be014b6c5d97a7d5b47555a2ae47450","13203d0b511337f023586d1fa57cfff1087beb4f","229ed2a61b5ac67ec65121182eb4090961f54ce3","2fb394d350360cb18a70b82065c0da7545d3be24","3a1b91d8c1114c9d84ce23702f45fe2ff3870503","2517b61d12a0d3d6b9833c115f038ecc1e948313"],"m":438},{"id":"flaglimits_p18_439","t":"Wes\n\nHi guys,\n\nI've been searching for FLs that bounced price on return. Tried to find examples which were clear and obvious to me. I've also read that Harry suggested to search for bullish and bearish ones seperately, so here are the first 5 bullish FLs that I found.\n\nComments and advice is always welcome if and when you guys have the time!","a":"—","d":"","n":"#439","p":18,"im":[],"m":439},{"id":"flaglimits_p18_440","t":"Aaron\n\nHey Wes,\n\nYou have the idea Good going!\n\n1707\n\nAaron","a":"—","d":"","n":"#440","p":18,"im":[],"m":440},{"id":"flaglimits_p18_441","t":"Wes\n\nIt's getting increasly easier to spot them. Which is noticable when you look at the charts at the bottom of this page. Here are a few bearish examples where price reacted on the first return:","a":"—","d":"","n":"#441","p":18,"im":["bc8d1208e045b5ba0c25dc8ea73311ca44d0a7c4","024f03590c06c06230042878b210118f2e02d5e5"],"m":441},{"id":"flaglimits_p18_442","t":"dcabfx\n\nSorry to just jump in Wes. To answer your question on one of your charts where you had a well drawn out FL and then it was broken and another FL was created, you identified a FTB and that's an excellent read pal. In this HW thread, it is said over and over that when looking for a FL, it is of importance to see it break something of significance which we call SR. Well, the break of a previous FL is of much importance!\n\nThe FL is extremely important and has several plays. Keep drilling through the charts looking for them and when they are respected and when the are broken.\n\nYour charts are clean and easy to read. Keeping it simple helped me lots. Keep 'em charts coming!\n\ndcabfx","a":"—","d":"","n":"#442","p":18,"im":[],"m":442},{"id":"flaglimits_p18_443","t":"Some more FL charts\n\nThis chart is the drilled down 1 H chart of the above 4 H chart.","a":"—","d":"","n":"#443","p":18,"im":["22dcb2cb835373cbe4aad2170ab2d8991375a9ca","5e225b5df613cc4c1edde96adf84e2ec8a421e74","b16f6a1ced61ef1051fbc4e0ceedc98c10770d2f","532d8f916cf1b90abc59c5cd6b13db9e49dfc22b","cbb94c4135064fe6e3643dca548de2fd973849dd","ff6644c62058f1998586a8a3f2e8b7c166854535","8e15d138156cd97e4bd2aafea13c055cc681e015"],"m":443},{"id":"flaglimits_p18_444","t":"Aaron\n\nHi Macbow,\n\nI have made a few remarks on one of you're charts mate, when studying it pays to be very meticulous, it helps me a lot.","a":"—","d":"","n":"#444","p":18,"im":[],"m":444},{"id":"flaglimits_p18_445","t":"Pedini\n\nThats really nice work from all you guys. It's exactly what we love to see!","a":"—","d":"","n":"#445","p":18,"im":[],"m":445},{"id":"flaglimits_p18_446","t":"rcmacf\n\nSomething I've been pondering..\n\nSo, surely what happens in 2 must be a reaction to something after area 3?","a":"—","d":"","n":"#446","p":18,"im":[],"m":446},{"id":"flaglimits_p18_447","t":"Wow thanks Aaron. You have helped me a bunch mate just with the couple of critiques you have done on my charts. I am extremely grateful!","a":"—","d":"","n":"#447","p":18,"im":[],"m":447},{"id":"flaglimits_p18_448","t":"Aaron\n\nM,\n\nYou're very welcome my friend\n\nRcmacf raised a really good point mate, I would definitely focus in on w